# Ring switching on the Rust's vector

Values printed by a test run on `crates/verifier/src/ring_switch.rs` at branch
`hotwire-dense-int` (a test module appended for the run, not committed): `frobenius`;
`Placement::stack_point` and `eq_above` on two placements (`variables = 5`, `index = 160`;
`variables = 3`, `index = 40`) in a stack of `2^10` words; and `ring_switch` on an unchecked
transcript, its challenges read off a twin transcript after the same grind (`samples_packed` of
`2·8 + 1` for one claim, `2·8 + 2` for two), its target and its weight at stack points. One claim
is one whole column, as `q_keccak`'s in the walk; the two claims share points across pieces and claims
and include a whole-stack piece (`placement: None`), so the point groups, `rho`'s scaling of the
slices and the scales, and `eq_above` all enter the weight. `ringMerge` is fed the challenges the
Rust drew. Each check is run compiled (`#guard`).
